.TH EZBIND 1 "2026-10-24" "ezbind 0.1.0-dev B2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ezbind \- prepare an ebook PDF for folded-folio home bookbinding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ezbind
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.I INPUT.pdf
.I OUTPUT.pdf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ezbind
reads a local input PDF and writes a duplex folded-folio arrangement in folio
mode. Each output sheet has two finished-page positions on each side. The
nominal folio assignment is front-left 4, front-right 1, back-left 2, and
back-right 3. Incomplete final folios are padded with blank logical pages.
.PP
Cover-only mode reads the supplied front and back SVG files and writes a
separate cover PDF without opening a text-block PDF. Combined mode generates
both folio and cover PDFs.
.PP
The canonical usage statement for folio mode and the first line of help and usage errors is:
.PP
.nf
Usage: ezbind [OPTIONS] INPUT.pdf OUTPUT.pdf
.fi
.PP
Folio and combined modes take exactly two positional paths. Cover-only mode
takes zero positional paths and requires --cover-front, --cover-back, and
--cover-output.
Options may be interspersed with positional paths; \fB--\fR ends option
parsing. Examples prefer options first. The input PDF and source SVGs must not
also be destinations, including normalized path aliases; folio and cover
destinations must differ.
.PP
Existing destinations are replaced without prompting only after successful
generation. The current B2 slice supports Letter and A4 sheets, an optional
margin grid, and separate SVG cover output. Physical cover cards, adhesive,
and fabric remain user-supplied.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help , \-h
Print usage, a concise option summary, and exit-status summary without requiring
an input PDF; return status 0.
.TP
.BR --sheet\~letter | \-s\~letter | --sheet\~a4 | \-s\~a4
Select the physical output sheet. Letter is the default. Output is landscape:
792 x 612 points for Letter and approximately 841.89 x 595.28 points for A4.
.TP
.BR --grid , \-g
Add light-gray vector grid lines in the margin areas. The default spacing is
5 mm. Grid lines are not added unless this option is selected.
.TP
.B --grid-spacing \fIVALUE\fR, -G \fIVALUE\fR
Set positive grid spacing in \fBmm\fR, \fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR; the default is
5 mm.
.TP
.BR --margin-top\~VALUE | \-t\~VALUE | --margin-bottom\~VALUE | \-b\~VALUE
Set top or bottom output clearance. Values require a non-negative \fBmm\fR,
\fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR suffix. Defaults are zero.
.TP
.BR --crop-top\~VALUE | --crop-bottom\~VALUE | --crop-left\~VALUE | --crop-right\~VALUE
Remove source-page edge distances before placement. Cropping may remove source
content but must leave positive page area. Values require a non-negative
\fBmm\fR, \fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR suffix and default to zero. Distances are
measured from the effective CropBox, falling back to MediaBox; edge names refer
to visual edges after rotation. Auto-crop is not enabled.
.TP
.BR --margin-fore-edge\~VALUE | \-e\~VALUE | --margin-spine\~VALUE | \-i\~VALUE
Set fore-edge or spine output clearance. The spine is the fold-facing inner
edge; the fore-edge is outer. Values require a non-negative \fBmm\fR, \fBin\fR,
or \fBpt\fR suffix. Both defaults are zero.
.TP
.B --cover-front \fIPATH\fR
SVG artwork for the front cover. Supply it together with --cover-back and
--cover-output.
.TP
.B --cover-back \fIPATH\fR
SVG artwork for the back cover, rendered on the left half of the landscape
cover sheet.
.TP
.B --cover-output \fIPATH\fR
Write a separate one-page cover PDF. Front artwork is rendered on the right
half and back artwork on the left. A dashed gray center cut guide is drawn over
the artwork, inset 12 points from the top and bottom edges. Artwork is fitted
proportionally to each half-sheet viewport.
.SH DEFAULT LAYOUT
Default minimum clearances are zero points at the top, bottom, fore-edge, and
spine. Source pages are fitted uniformly inside the resulting content
rectangle without distortion. Source crop options are applied before this fit.
Aspect-ratio differences may leave additional letterboxing. The optional grid
occupies reserved strips and does not cross source content. A one-page source
produces two physical output sides; source counts are padded to multiples of
four.
.SH OUTPUT AND PHYSICAL WORKFLOW
Print duplex using the printer setting appropriate for the selected paper. Fold
each sheet once with the fold toward the spine, keep the generated folio order,
and stack before gluing the spine side. Confirm duplex orientation with a small
asymmetric fixture before committing a valuable book.
.PP
When cover mode is selected, print the separate cover PDF on the selected
cardstock size. The back artwork is on the left and the front artwork is on the
right; cut along the dashed gray center guide so both cut edges face the spine.
The guide is inset 12 points from the sheet edges. Cover artwork is rendered by
librsvg onto a Cairo PDF surface and fitted proportionally to each half-sheet
viewport.
.PP
Existing folio and cover outputs are replaced without prompting only after
successful generation. Outputs are first written to sibling temporary files;
a handled failure does not leave temporary output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Input PDF error, including unreadable, malformed, or empty input.
.TP
.B 4
Impossible layout.
.TP
.B 5
Output or filesystem error.
.TP
.B 6
Missing or unusable runtime dependency.
.TP
.B 10
Unexpected internal processing error.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Usage errors are written to standard error and include the diagnostic followed
by the canonical usage line. Ordinary diagnostics do not include extracted
source text, passwords, or complete PDF content.
.SH PDF LIMITATIONS
The qpdf backend preserves visible page content and selectable text for the
implemented folio placement path. Cover artwork is rendered through librsvg
2.58 and Cairo; unsupported SVG features, external resources, and font
availability can affect output and must be validated against representative
artwork. Spine/fabric guides, auto-crop, crop/fold/registration marks, creep,
printer safe-area configuration, and broad document-feature capability
reporting are not yet exposed by this B2 slice. Source-page annotations and
form fields may not follow clipped content.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
ezbind --sheet a4 --grid book.pdf book-bound.pdf
.fi
.PP
Generate a folio and separate cover sheet:
.PP
.nf
ezbind --sheet letter --cover-back back.svg --cover-front front.svg \\
  --cover-output covers.pdf book.pdf book-bound.pdf
.fi
.PP
Generate a cover without a text-block PDF:
.PP
.nf
ezbind --sheet letter --cover-back back.svg \\
  --cover-front front.svg --cover-output covers.pdf
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qpdf (1)
